  "description": "Subject: Configuration Summary for GSLB Service Group Binding \u2013 gslb_service_group1  \n\nThe server identified as **srv-001** is bound to the GSLB service group **groupA** under the name **gslb_service_group1**. Its primary IP address is **192.168.1.10** (service IP string also 192.168.1.10) and it listens on **TCP port\u202f443**. A duplicate service is configured as **HTTP** on **port\u202f8080**. AppFlow logging is **enabled**, while client IP insertion is **disabled**; the header that would be used for client IP forwarding is **X-Forwarded-For**. The client timeout is set to **180\u202fseconds**, the server timeout to **60\u202fseconds**, and the down\u2011state flush behavior is **enabled**. The server\u2019s current state is **UP**, with no configuration flags set (**svrcfgflags\u202f=\u202f0**).  \n\nResource limits for this binding include a maximum bandwidth of **1000** (units), a maximum of **200** concurrent clients, and a request ceiling of **5000**. The monitor threshold is configured at **100**, and the binding count stands at **5**. All values reflect the current configuration and no further changes are required.",
